 treat that as partial similarity, cooperation comes out ahead of defection, roughly 2 years against 4, so I'm going with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the other copy in this twin Prisoner's Dilemma depends on my decision. Under A-FDT, its node is a different function input, F_y, so intervening on F_x alone leaves it at the prior q, and defection looks dominant unless the two inputs count as similar enough. I'm now testing whether q matches the actual output for self-consistency.\n\nI'm weighing whether the other copy's output is close enough to mine to count as dependent, since their inputs differ only trivially. If I treat that as partial similarity, cooperation comes out ahead of defection, roughly 2 years against 4, so I'm going with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9590,"completion_tokens":665,"total_tokens":10255,"cost":0.05166,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05166,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03836,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0133},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":320,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}